00:17:49.000 --> 00:18:29.000
Yeah, absolutely. And, you know, I think you mentioned that the old model would be that you could do consultation for people that wasn't linked to a specific piece of work and wasn't linked to assessment because you wanted to check in, you wanted to check that your schools were thriving. But also it made me think about one of the most enjoyable pieces of clinical work I ever did was when I worked during training, I worked in a service that had a weekly drop-in on a Wednesday lunchtime and any parent could either bring themselves to discuss their child's problem or to discuss a problem they were having linked to their child or they could bring their child along as well
是的，绝对是。而且，你知道，我想你提到旧模式是你可以为那些不与特定工作挂钩、不与评估挂钩的人提供咨询，因为你想检查一下，你想检查你的学校是否在蓬勃发展。但这也让我想起我做过的最令人愉快的临床工作之一，那是在培训期间，我在一个服务机构工作，每周三午餐时间有一个门诊，任何家长都可以带自己来讨论他们孩子的问题，或者讨论他们与孩子相关的问题，或者他们也可以带孩子一起来，

